{"id": "3997eb09-450b-4500-9a23-5b64c7a511b1", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T14:21:56.409081", "source": "user", "parent_id": "fc639b70-2347-41b1-965f-a71a68d4ddb6", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Initial inspection request for design-only study on SiT with non-causal Hyena time operator. Please perform the following and report back; do NOT yet produce the final experiment design. (1) Repository inspection: list the contents of /workspace at the top two directory levels, identify any existing code, papers, notes, or SiT/Hyena-related references already present, and report whether the workspace is empty or contains prior materials relevant to the SiT architecture, Hyena operators, or long-horizon trajectory modelling. (2) Proposed approach: sketch a concise candidate experimental design that answers the central question—whether replacing the time attention mechanism with a non-causal Hyena operator in SiT allows the model to generate extremely long, consistent trajectories capturing dynamics over multiple timescales. The sketch should briefly indicate the two configurations being compared (SiT with original time attention vs. SiT with non-causal Hyena operator), candidate datasets or trajectory types (video, motion, physical dynamics, or synthetic multi-timescale sequences), the candidate primary metrics (long-horizon consistency, multi-timescale fidelity, computational cost, training stability), and the high-level controls (matched parameter count or matched FLOPs, matched training schedule, identical conditioning). (3) Assumptions and uncertainties: explicitly list the consequential assumptions you would need to make to finalise the design—expected empirical outcome, available compute and runtime budget, choice of dataset and sequence length, definition of 'extremely long' and 'multiple timescales', non-causality handling at inference, evaluation protocol, and any setup detail not present in available context. Flag any item that can only be resolved by researcher clarification. Keep this turn focused on inspection and proposal only; await my review before drafting the final design.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Does replacing the time attention mechanism with a non-causal Hyena operator in the SiT architecture allow the model to generate extremely long, consistent trajectories that capture dynamics over multiple timescales?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/93022/6:setup_4\", \"neurips2024/93022/6:setup_5\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
