lot degradation and locate where Hyena's sub-quadratic cost diverges from attention.\\n\\n### Candidate primary metrics\\n\\n| Pillar | Metric | Why |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Long-horizon consistency | (a) rollout forecast skill (RMSE / NLL) at multiple horizons vs. analytic truth / held-out future; (b) spectral / multi-timescale fidelity (per-band PSD error, log-power-spectrum MSE, autocorrelation consistency at multiple lags) | directly answers \\\"consistent\\\" and \\\"multiple timescales\\\" |\\n| Multi-timescale fidelity | per-timescale PSD/MSE after band-pass decomposition; phase coherence; Wasserstein-1 on returns | isolates where one operator beats the other |\\n| Computational cost | wall-clock per training step; params; FLOPs; activation memory vs. sequence length | one of the purported benefits of Hyena; required for matched-cost control |\\n| Training stability | gradient-norm curves, loss curves, NaN/Inf events, effective rank of features | non-causal mixing can change optimisation landscape |\\n\\nA single scalar primary endpoint (e.g., summed log-PSD error at the longest horizon across timescale bands); others as secondary/supporting. Needs your call.\\n\\n### Controls (high-level)\\n\\n- Matched FLOPs (likely — with #params reported separately) as the headline cost-control.\\n- Matched training schedule: same optimiser, lr schedule, warm-up, total tokens/steps, batch size, seed, mixed-precision.\\n- Identical conditioning: same noise schedule (DDPM / flow-matching), same conditioning inputs, same sampling (same NFE, same solver).\\n- Identical spatial mixing and everything else except the time-axis operator.\\n- Worth including if budget allows: causal vs. non-causal Hyena sub-arm (separates \\\"Hyena\\\" vs. \\\"non-causality\\\"); train-short / eval-long vs. train-long / eval-long.\\n\\n### Sub-questions the experiment should answer\\n1. Does SiT-Hyena match SiT-TimeAttn in multi-timescale fidelity at short horizons?\\n2. Where does their relative err